## Round 4d — Lab entry: pinned action bar, panels add all their tests, automatic flag (owner 2026-11-01, D20/D21)
Owner words: the Next/Save buttons must stay in place and always be reachable; picking a panel (e.g. preeclampsia) must bring ALL its tests, not one; unit and reference range are small light text, not their own wide boxes; Normal/Abnormal is worked out from the reference range (TSH and similar do not suit buttons). Scope: lab entry screen only. NOT in this round: the on-screen number keypad of the mock-up (needs owner sign-off), medication/ultrasound/other editors (they must look and behave exactly as today), settings.
Finding behind the panel bug: the lab draft holds ONE test, and a panel chip only filtered the list of test chips, so no panel ever added its tests; the lookup was also case-sensitive.

Q240 (NEW model/LabResultFlag.kt) ONE pure function `fun labResultFlag(result: String, referenceRange: String): LabResultFlag` and `enum class LabResultFlag { NORMAL, HIGH, LOW, UNKNOWN }`. Both inputs trimmed. Range forms: `a - b` (also en dash, any spaces; a<=b), `< x`, `<= x`, `> x`, `>= x`, decimal point only. Result must be a plain number (optional decimal part); anything else (text, empty, "<5", "5.0 g/dL") -> UNKNOWN; range unparsable or empty -> UNKNOWN. `a - b`: below a -> LOW, above b -> HIGH, inclusive ends NORMAL. `< x`: result < x NORMAL, otherwise HIGH. `<= x`: result <= x NORMAL else HIGH. `> x`: result > x NORMAL, otherwise LOW. `>= x` likewise. Never a clinical threshold of its own: only the stored range decides.
Q241 (model/codex/ClinicalCodexModels.kt) ONE pure function `fun resolveLabPanel(panel: LabCategoryGroup, items: List<LabCodexItem>): LabPanelResolution` and `data class LabPanelResolution(val tests: List<LabCodexItem>, val missing: List<String>)`. `tests` follows the panel's `testNames` order, each name matched to an item ignoring case and surrounding spaces, no item twice; names without an item go to `missing` (order kept). Every default panel (`ClinicalCodexRepository.defaultLabCategoryGroups()`) resolves with `missing` empty against `defaultLabCodexItems()`.
Q242 (ui/PatientEditor.kt `EditorPage`) new optional parameter `bottomBar: (@Composable () -> Unit)? = null` (default null = layout exactly as today for every other editor). When set, the bar is drawn BELOW the scrolling content, outside it, always visible, above the keyboard (imePadding), with a divider/surface in theme colours; the content area above it scrolls. Only LabEditor passes it.
Q243 (ui/LabEditor.kt) the bottom bar holds Cancel (`cancelLab`), "+ Add another test" (`addAnotherLab`) and Save (`saveLab`): same events and tags as today, 48 dp, no wrapping text, remaining on one row at 130 % font (use a Row with weights, or wrap only when needed). They no longer sit in the scrolling content.
Q244 (ui/LabEditor.kt) panels: tapping a panel chip starts a queue made with `resolveLabPanel` (the "Panel Tests" chip list also uses it): the first test is loaded into the draft with the SAME function the test chips use (one function that copies category, name, default result, unit and range into the draft; the chips and the queue both call it, no second copy). While the queue has tests left the screen shows "Test X of Y: <name>" with a thin progress bar and the add-another button reads "Save and next test"; after a successful chained save the next queued test is loaded into the new chained draft; leaving the screen or tapping the panel chip again clears the queue; a save that fails does not advance it. `missing` names are ignored silently. Tapping a single test chip still loads just that test (and clears the queue). Date and laboratory name stay set across the batch as today.
Q245 (ui/LabEditor.kt) result/flag/range: unit and reference range are shown as one light line under the result field ("mg/dL · ref 11.0 - 15.0"; nothing when both are empty) with a small text button "Edit unit and range" that reveals the two existing fields (`labUnit`, `labRefRange`, unchanged tags); when both are empty the two fields are shown directly (a custom test needs them). Whenever the result or the range changes and `labResultFlag` is not UNKNOWN, the existing event `LabAbnormalChanged(flag != NORMAL)` is sent; UNKNOWN leaves the abnormal choice as the doctor set it. A small pill next to the result shows "Normal", "High" or "Low" (theme colours: error colour for High/Low, not colour alone: the word is always shown). The abnormal switch (`labAbnormal`) stays as the override but is compact (one line). Draft saving, validation, fields and stored record format are unchanged.
Static checks (.agents/checks/check_r4d.py; strip comments; main sources only):
 S140 `fun labResultFlag` defined once in model/LabResultFlag.kt, `fun resolveLabPanel` defined once in ClinicalCodexModels.kt; LabEditor.kt calls both; neither rule is re-implemented in the UI (no regex over the range text in ui/).
 S141 `EditorPage` has a `bottomBar` parameter defaulting to null; LabEditor.kt is the only file that passes `bottomBar`; in LabEditor.kt the tags cancelLab, addAnotherLab and saveLab each occur once and after the `bottomBar` argument.
 S142 these tags are all still present in LabEditor.kt: labNameField labDate labName labResult labUnit labRefRange labAbnormal labNotes allLabTestsChip labGroupChip- labPreset labResultPreset labCategoryChoice saveToLabCodexBanner saveToLabCodexButton; no visible "Codex" literal in LabEditor.kt.
Unit (JVM): NEW model/LabResultFlagTest.kt: range a-b (below, inside, both ends, above, en dash, spaces), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, decimals, text result, empty result, "<5" result, empty and junk range -> UNKNOWN. NEW model/codex/LabPanelResolveTest.kt: every default panel resolves with nothing missing (regression for "preeclampsia panel gave only TSH"); order follows the panel; case-insensitive; unknown name goes to missing; same test not twice; a renamed test (after applyLabItemEdit) still resolves in its panel.
